  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Protecting journalists to protect democracy: tackling emergency threat</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project targets five regions (Latin America, Africa, Arab States, Europe, Asia), to provide a holistic approach to advancing the safety of journalists and protecting democracy. The project will work on four key outcomes: 
1.Supporting normative frameworks and programme initiatives that address the situation of journalists in crisis contexts; 2.Creating an enabling environment for freedom of expression and safety of journalists during electoral processes 3.Reinforcing the resilience and safety of journalists in at least 10 countries, with a focus on tackling digital and legal attacks 4.Women journalists have enhanced skills to deal with specific gendered threats</narrative>
  </description>
